  "anchor": "Plan v27 Lane A.5 — per-sector classification used by the 4-factor extrapolation formula. urban_factor categorizes how concentrated this sector is in cities ('high', 'neutral', 'low' = rural-dominant). corruption_exposure flags whether reported revenue tracks true revenue tightly ('low') or whether shadow-economy + bribery skew the picture ('high'). tradability is whether the output crosses borders easily ('global', 'regional', 'local'). sector_elasticity is the GDP-per-capita elasticity: 1.0 = revenue scales linearly with GDP, 2.0 = revenue scales much faster than GDP (software in rich countries earns vastly more than in poor ones), 0.5 = revenue scales much slower (a haircut costs roughly the same everywhere as a share of local wages).",
